	"crit_shining_mewtoo": {"stats": [["DESIGNED BY", "Ken Sugimoori"], ["FIRST GAME", "Pocket Critters Red and Blue (1996)"], ["FIRST SEEN", "first generation of Pocket Critters"], ["SPECIES", "Pocket Critters"], ["TYPE", "Psychic"]], "hist": [["THE LOWDOWN", "Mewtoo is a Pocket Critters species in Funtendo and Game Freek's Pocket Critters media franchise. It was first introduced in the video games Pocket Critters Red and Blue, and later appeared in subsequent sequels and spin-off titles, such as Pokkén Tournament and Detective Pikapal."], ["ORIGIN", "Standing 6 feet 7 inches (201 cm) tall, it appears as a bipedal feline."], ["IN THE GAME", "Mewtoo also appears in the film Pocket Critters: Mewtoo Strikes Back—Evolution, a remake of Pocket Critters: The First Movie, that premiered on July 12, 2019."], ["RECEPTION", "While it has been cited as a \"complex and compelling villain\" by some critics, its goal of world domination was received as a trait shared by \"…every anime villain…\", and likened to a James Bond villain by Daily Record."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "Mewtoo also appears as a usable Pocket Critters in Pocket Critters Mastors as the partner of Giovanni, who first became playable in the first Legendary Event, \"Lurking Shadow\"."], ["ONE MORE THING", "Brawl, Mewtoo returned to the series as a DLC character in Super Bash Bros. for Funtendo 3DS and Wee U on April 28, 2015, though it was made available to Club Funtendo members who registered both versions on April 15, 2015."]], "year": 0},
