	"crit_laprass": {"stats": [["FIRST SEEN", "first generation of Pocket Critters"]], "hist": [["THE LOWDOWN", "Created by Ken Sugimori, Laprasss first appeared in the video games Pocket Critters Red and Blue and subsequent sequels, later appearing in various merchandise, spinoff titles and animated and printed adaptations of the franchise."], ["ORIGIN", "In Pocket Critters Sword and Shield, Laprasss received a Gigantamax form with access to the unique G-Max Move G-Max Resonance, the only Ice-type G-Max Move."], ["RECEPTION", "In 2016, a man crashed his car after seeing a Laprasss that he hadn’t encountered before, and in 2017, a Singaporean player named Liang Weiming died from a heart attack after capturing a rare Laprasss at Marina Bay Sands."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "Laprasss is most known for its fondness of moving people and Pocket Critters across bodies of water."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "In the Pocket Critters of the Year poll held by Critter Co, Laprasss was voted the tenth most popular Generation I Pocket Critters, receiving 23,411 votes."]], "year": 0},
