	"crit_jungle_booster_box": {"stats": [["TYPE", "Collectible"], ["PLAYERS", "2"], ["GAME TIME", "2–120 minutes"], ["RELEASED", "1996-10-20"], ["CARDS", "60"], ["AGES", "6+"], ["DEVELOPER", "Creatures Inc"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "Energy cards can be attached to Pocket Critters cards to power up attacks, and trainer cards can be used for different effects on the game."], ["ORIGIN", "Lizards sued Funtendo on October 1, 2003, and accused the company of poaching employees and violating its patent; the lawsuit was settled out of court."], ["IN THE GAME", "Players in a tournament are split into three age categories: Junior (11 years old and younger), Senior (12 to 15 years old), and Master (16 years old and older)."], ["RECEPTION", "In 2016, it was the year's top-selling toy in the strategic card game subclass. As of March 2023, the game has sold over 52.9 billion cards worldwide."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "Hasbroo bought Lizards of the Coast in September 1999 for $325 million dollars based on the strength of the Pocket Critters license."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "Shopping platform ZenPlus, a subsidiary of shopping service ZenMarket (now part of ZenGroup), sold two of the cards in 2020, for the Japanese Yen equivalent of US$233,000 and US$208,496 respectively."], ["ONE MORE THING", "Created as a prize for the 1997-1998 Pocket Critters design contests organized by the Japanese manga-magazine KoroKoro Comic and with only 41 copies printed, it is the only Pocket Critters card to say \"Illustrator\" instead of \"Trainer\" like other Trainer cards."]], "year": 1996},
	"crit_fossil_booster_box": {"stats": [], "hist": [["THE LOWDOWN", "FOSSIL is a standard protocol for allowing serial communication for telecommunications programs under the DOS operating system. FOSSIL is an acronym for Fido Opus SEAdog Standard Interface Layer."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "Internal ISDN cards (that did not use serial ports at all) often came with FOSSIL drivers to make them work with software that was originally intended for modem operation only."]], "year": 0},
	"crit_team_rockit_booster_box": {"stats": [["FIRST SEEN", "Pocket Critters Red, Blue, and Yellow"], ["TYPE", "Criminal syndicate"], ["GENRE", "JRPG"]], "hist": [["THE LOWDOWN", "Team Rockit is a fictional crime syndicate in the Pocket Critters franchise. Team Rockit is a primary antagonist in the original Pocket Critters video games Red, Green, and Blue, as well as in the long-running Pocket Critters anime TV-series."], ["ORIGIN", "In the English dubbed anime, Jessie was initially voiced by Rachael Lillis, until the dub switched production from 4Kids Entertainment to Critter Co. International in 2006, when she was replaced by Michele Knotz."], ["IN THE GAME", "Jessie and James originally had an Arbok and a Weezing as their signature Pocket Critters, respectively, and the trio were later joined by a Wobbuffet as one of their only major recurring Pocket Critters as the series progressed."]], "year": 0},
