	"crit_mewl": {"stats": [["CREATED BY", "Shigeki Morimotoo"], ["FIRST GAME", "Pocket Critters Red and Blue (1996)"], ["FIRST SEEN", "first generation of Pocket Critters"], ["SPECIES", "Pocket Critters"], ["TYPE", "Psychic"]], "hist": [["THE LOWDOWN", "Mewl is one of the many fictional species in the Pocket Critters franchise. It is a small, pink, Psychic-type Mythical Pocket Critters, which are incredibly rare and powerful Pocket Critters typically available only via special events."], ["ORIGIN", "During initial distributions for Mewl, the pool of those who would potentially receive one was relatively small—numbering only twenty in the first and one hundred in the second—due to the fact that each Mewl had to be individually generated on Morimotoo's PC and then manually traded to winning cartridges."], ["IN THE GAME", "At the time of its introduction, Mewl could only be legitimately obtained in the Pocket Critters video games via Funtendo promotional event distributions."], ["RECEPTION", "In 2021, Oreos depicting Pocket Critters characters were released, with those depicting Mewl being particularly rare and sought after by fans of the series, leading to bids on sales of the cookie jumping up to prices as high as several thousand dollars."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "In Pocket Critters Sun and Moon, a special \"Z-Crystal\" item was created for Mewl, which allowed it to use a powerful attack only it could use, known as \"Genesys Supernova\"."]], "year": 0},
