	"crit_digglet": {"stats": [["TYPE", "Collectible"], ["PLAYERS", "2"], ["GAME TIME", "2–120 minutes"], ["RELEASED", "1996-10-20"], ["CARDS", "60"], ["AGES", "6+"], ["DEVELOPER", "Creatures Inc"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "Basic (unevolved) Pocket Critters can change into their evolved forms during the game by playing subsequent evolution cards in the deck."], ["ORIGIN", "Lizards sued Funtendo on October 1, 2003, and accused the company of poaching employees and violating its patent; the lawsuit was settled out of court."], ["IN THE GAME", "The first version of Pocket Critters Play It! was released in 1999, followed by its sequel Pocket Critters Play It! The first Pocket Critters TCG tournament began on June 14–15, 1997, at the Makuhari Messe Event Hall."], ["RECEPTION", "In 2017, it had an 82% share of Europe's strategic card game market. As of March 2023, the game has sold over 52.9 billion cards worldwide."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "Shopping platform ZenPlus, a subsidiary of shopping service ZenMarket (now part of ZenGroup), sold two of the cards in 2020, for the Japanese Yen equivalent of US$233,000 and US$208,496 respectively."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "The \"1st Starter & Expansion Pack\" contained various Pocket Critters cards depicting the original 150 Pocket Critters species in the main Pocket Critters franchise, and it is the only expansion not to have a set logo or symbol (i.e. except for the error \"no-symbol\" Jungle cards)."], ["ONE MORE THING", "A third card was sold on the platform in 2022 for US$772,000."]], "year": 1996},
	"magi_mocks_jet": {"stats": [["BIG SALE", "$27,302"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "These nine cards were printed in the first sets of Magick: The Gatherening, starting in 1993."], ["ORIGIN", "When tournaments were officially organized, a list of banned and restricted cards was created for the various formats; the Moxen were restricted to one copy each per deck."], ["RECEPTION", "A Bleak Lotus card signed by Richard Garfield with a grade of 6 from Beckit was sold for $72,000. In March 2022, a mint condition Alpha edition Mocks Emerald sold for $29,999."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "In 2022, Post Malone paid $800,000 for an artist's proof signed by artist Christopher Rush. Bleak Lotus is usually considered by collectors to be the most valuable non-promotional Magic card due to its limited print and limited distribution."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "The Power Nine represent the rarest and most expensive collectible Magick: The Gatherening cards."], ["ONE MORE THING", "There were 22,800 copies of the card printed overall, about 1,100 in the Alpha edition, and about 3,300 in the Beta edition."]], "year": 0},
	"magi_mocks_ruby": {"stats": [["BIG SALE", "$27,302"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "The cards were added to Magick: The Gatherening Arena in September 2022 with the introduction of the Alchemy: Dominaria United expansion set."], ["ORIGIN", "These nine cards were printed in the first sets of Magick: The Gatherening, starting in 1993. There were 22,800 copies of the card printed overall, about 1,100 in the Alpha edition, and about 3,300 in the Beta edition."], ["RECEPTION", "A Bleak Lotus card signed by Richard Garfield with a grade of 6 from Beckit was sold for $72,000. In March 2022, a mint condition Alpha edition Mocks Emerald sold for $29,999."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "The Power Nine represent the rarest and most expensive collectible Magick: The Gatherening cards. Bleak Lotus is usually considered by collectors to be the most valuable non-promotional Magic card due to its limited print and limited distribution."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "Owing to their power, they were banned from being played in most competitive settings."], ["ONE MORE THING", "The card's standing in the Magic: the Gathering community is evinced by the creation of the Magick: The Gatherening Players Tour, which was originally established as the Bleak Lotus Pro Tour and first contested in February 1996 in New York City."]], "year": 0},
	"magi_mocks_pearl": {"stats": [["BIG SALE", "$27,302"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "The cards were added to Magick: The Gatherening Arena in September 2022 with the introduction of the Alchemy: Dominaria United expansion set."], ["ORIGIN", "When tournaments were officially organized, a list of banned and restricted cards was created for the various formats; the Moxen were restricted to one copy each per deck."], ["RECEPTION", "From January to August 2022, there were 122 Power Nine cards sold at auction, of which 21 were from Alpha, 30 were from Beta, and 71 were from Unlimited. In March 2022, a mint condition Alpha edition Mocks Emerald sold for $29,999."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "Bleak Lotus is usually considered by collectors to be the most valuable non-promotional Magic card due to its limited print and limited distribution. In 2022, Post Malone paid $800,000 for an artist's proof signed by artist Christopher Rush."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "The card's standing in the Magic: the Gathering community is evinced by the creation of the Magick: The Gatherening Players Tour, which was originally established as the Bleak Lotus Pro Tour and first contested in February 1996 in New York City."], ["ONE MORE THING", "As of 2022 Beckit Media has graded 263 copies of the Alpha edition of Bleak Lotus, and Professional Sports Authenticator (PZA) has graded 110."]], "year": 0},
	"magi_mocks_emerald": {"stats": [["BIG SALE", "$27,302"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "The cards were added to Magick: The Gatherening Arena in September 2022 with the introduction of the Alchemy: Dominaria United expansion set."], ["ORIGIN", "When tournaments were officially organized, a list of banned and restricted cards was created for the various formats; the Moxen were restricted to one copy each per deck."], ["RECEPTION", "In 2013, one version of the card sold for $27,302. From January to August 2022, there were 122 Power Nine cards sold at auction, of which 21 were from Alpha, 30 were from Beta, and 71 were from Unlimited."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "In March 2022, a mint condition Alpha edition Mocks Emerald sold for $29,999. Bleak Lotus is usually considered by collectors to be the most valuable non-promotional Magic card due to its limited print and limited distribution."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "In 2022, Post Malone paid $800,000 for an artist's proof signed by artist Christopher Rush."], ["ONE MORE THING", "A Bleak Lotus card signed by Richard Garfield with a grade of 6 from Beckit was sold for $72,000."]], "year": 0},
