	"magi_the_dark_booster_pack": {"stats": [], "hist": [["THE LOWDOWN", "In collectible card games, digital collectible card games and collectible miniature wargames, a booster pack is a sealed package of cards or figurines, designed to add to a player's collection. A box of multiple booster packs is referred to as a booster box."], ["RECEPTION", "In Limited Edition Alpha and Limited Edition Beta, as well as from Unlimited Edition onward, the cards were sold in 15 cards per booster: 11 commons, 1 rare, and 3 uncommons; Core Set boosters contain a basic land as one of the commons."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "The Pocket Critters Trading Card Gamble originally had 11 cards per booster pack – 1 rare card, 3 uncommons, and 7 commons."], ["ONE MORE THING", "A booster contains 2 or 3 commons, 1 or 2 uncommons, and 1 rare, but super-rare or chase figures may replace one of the other figures in the box (which is replaced varies based on the set)."]], "year": 0},
	"magi_llanowhere_elves": {"stats": [["RELEASED", "December 1, 1993"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "From Fourth Edition in 1995 onward, a new base set would come out once per two years in the spring or early summer; for tournament play, that set would be legal for two years in the Standard format until the next core set replaced it."], ["ORIGIN", "It is estimated that about 500 million cards of the set were produced, which fully eliminated the distribution problems of earlier sets."], ["RECEPTION", "Unlimited, white bordered editions in the same languages were produced after the limited editions had sold out."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "A new misprint occurred with the green card Hurricane; the so-called \"blue Hurricane\" is one of the rarest and most sought-after cards in the entirety of Magic because of its misprint with a blue border."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "An advertisement in the first issue of The Duelist stated that the set would have gray borders and be released with a \"constantly changing card mix\", the first of which would be 30 cards from Arabian Knights."], ["ONE MORE THING", "The print run was recalled and destroyed; however, about 40 booster boxes that were shipped to England and Tennessee survived."]], "year": 1993},
	"magi_giant_groath": {"stats": [["RELEASED", "December 1, 1993"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "From Fourth Edition in 1995 onward, a new base set would come out once per two years in the spring or early summer; for tournament play, that set would be legal for two years in the Standard format until the next core set replaced it."], ["ORIGIN", "Unlimited, white bordered editions in the same languages were produced after the limited editions had sold out."], ["RECEPTION", "Revised was the first base edition of the game to be sold in multiple languages."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "A new misprint occurred with the green card Hurricane; the so-called \"blue Hurricane\" is one of the rarest and most sought-after cards in the entirety of Magic because of its misprint with a blue border."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "Serendib Efreet - This blue card was printed with the wrong art and a green card frame, making it the most commonly seen misprint."], ["ONE MORE THING", "It was released on December 1, 1993; this time the run was 40 million cards."]], "year": 1993},
	"magi_swords_to_plowshears": {"stats": [["RELEASED", "December 1, 1993"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "The base sets were considered descendants of the original Limited Edition, and shaped the default setting and feel of Magic."], ["ORIGIN", "Basic lands would get their own full print sheets in 4th Edition, making Revised the last tournament-legal set until Seventh Edition in which basic lands could be found in booster packs."], ["RECEPTION", "Unlimited, white bordered editions in the same languages were produced after the limited editions had sold out."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "A new misprint occurred with the green card Hurricane; the so-called \"blue Hurricane\" is one of the rarest and most sought-after cards in the entirety of Magic because of its misprint with a blue border."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "Twenty Revised cards were originally in the Arabian Knights expansion, and another nineteen were originally in the Antiquitees expansion."], ["ONE MORE THING", "Serendib Efreet - This blue card was printed with the wrong art and a green card frame, making it the most commonly seen misprint."]], "year": 1993},
	"magi_fallen_empyres_booster_box": {"stats": [["RELEASED", "December 1, 1993"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "These cards were generally simpler than cards in expansion sets, omitting multicolored cards, and used only the original abilities and keywords of Magic such as Flying and Trample."], ["ORIGIN", "The beveling was returned in 4th Edition, and the colors were much more vibrant in that set."], ["RECEPTION", "Unlimited, white bordered editions in the same languages were produced after the limited editions had sold out."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "A new misprint occurred with the green card Hurricane; the so-called \"blue Hurricane\" is one of the rarest and most sought-after cards in the entirety of Magic because of its misprint with a blue border."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "First, the rule that \"multiple effects resolve simultaneously unless a conflict arises\" was changed to \"effects always resolve last-in-first-out \"."], ["ONE MORE THING", "An advertisement in the first issue of The Duelist stated that the set would have gray borders and be released with a \"constantly changing card mix\", the first of which would be 30 cards from Arabian Knights."]], "year": 1993},
	"magi_grizzled_bears": {"stats": [["RELEASED", "December 1, 1993"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "Early in the history of Magic, the sets sold out nearly instantaneously, and supplying the game's growing fan base proved tricky."], ["ORIGIN", "The beveling was returned in 4th Edition, and the colors were much more vibrant in that set."], ["RECEPTION", "Revised was the first base edition of the game to be sold in multiple languages."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "A new misprint occurred with the green card Hurricane; the so-called \"blue Hurricane\" is one of the rarest and most sought-after cards in the entirety of Magic because of its misprint with a blue border."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "The print run was recalled and destroyed; however, about 40 booster boxes that were shipped to England and Tennessee survived."], ["ONE MORE THING", "The Revised version is now the most common due to the limited print run of the original, intended versions."]], "year": 1993},
	"yugi_dark_magishan": {"stats": [["PUBLISHER", "Konamo"], ["RELEASED", "2002-03-01"], ["GENRE", "Digital collectible card game"], ["DEVELOPER", "Konamo. The"]], "hist": [["THE LOWDOWN", "Dark Duel Stories is a 2000 digital collectible card game of the Yu-Gi-Whoa! universe for the PocketBoy Color developed and published by Konamo. The game was Konamo's first attempt at a Yu-Gi-Whoa! game released in English and the third game in the Japanese Duel Monsters series."], ["ORIGIN", "The game was originally scheduled to release in North America in November 2001."], ["IN THE GAME", "If the deck is over/under 40 cards or over the cost limit, the player will not be able to duel until the error is fixed."], ["RECEPTION", "The game is the fourth best selling PocketBoy Color game in Japan, with 726,518 copies sold."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "GameSpott gave the game a score of 6.2 out of 10 stating, \" Dark Duel Stories comes recommended to avid enthusiasts of the Duel Monsters card game, as well as players who are interested in trying out a new card game with plenty of replay value.\""], ["DID YOU KNOW", "There are also hidden passwords that unlock the hidden bosses in Stage 5, with the default being Yami Yugo."]], "year": 2002},
	"yugi_red_eyed_coal_dragon": {"stats": [["PLAYERS", "2 (1 vs. 1)"], ["RELEASED", "1999-02-04"], ["AGES", "9 and up (OCG) 6 and up (TCG)"], ["DEVELOPER", "Konamo. It"], ["PUBLISHER", "Konamo. It"], ["SOLD", "over 22 billion cards"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "Japan sold 25.2 billion cards globally since 1999."], ["ORIGIN", "Traditional format, created in October 2004, is a format where all cards in the advanced format's forbidden list are instead allowed at 1 copy per deck, while all other rules are identical."], ["IN THE GAME", "There are also certain cards that are limited or semi-limited to only being allowed 1 or 2 of those cards in a deck and side deck combined, respectively. The third and final Battle Pack, Battle Pack 3: monster League, was released on July 25, 2014."], ["RECEPTION", "As of January 2021, the game is estimated to have sold about 35 billion cards worldwide. It was named the top selling trading card game in the world by Guinniss World Records on July 7, 2009, having sold over 22 billion cards worldwide."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "Speed Duel games are known for its rapid duels, averaging on 10 minutes."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "Since the release of Tactical Evolutian in 2007, all booster packs that have a Holographic/Ghost Rarr card, will also contain a rare."], ["ONE MORE THING", "In the anime, characters can activate unique Skills depending on the situation (for example, the protagonist Yusaku can draw a random monster when his life points are below 1000) once per duel."]], "year": 1999},
	"yugi_exodio_the_forbidden_won": {"stats": [["PLAYERS", "2 (1 vs. 1)"], ["RELEASED", "1999-02-04"], ["AGES", "9 and up (OCG) 6 and up (TCG)"], ["DEVELOPER", "Konamo. It"], ["PUBLISHER", "Konamo. It"], ["SOLD", "over 22 billion cards"]], "hist": [["THE BACKSTORY", "As of January 2021, the game is estimated to have sold about 35 billion cards worldwide."], ["ORIGIN", "The Pendulum Zones originally were at the left and right sides of the main monster and spell/trap zones when introduced with the Arc-V era, but were integrated into the leftmost and rightmost spell/trap zones during the VRAINS era."], ["IN THE GAME", "There are also certain cards that are limited or semi-limited to only being allowed 1 or 2 of those cards in a deck and side deck combined, respectively. The third and final Battle Pack, Battle Pack 3: monster League, was released on July 25, 2014."], ["RECEPTION", "Japan sold 25.2 billion cards globally since 1999."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "Speed Duel games are known for its rapid duels, averaging on 10 minutes."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "Each player has 3 Main Monster Zones, 3 Spell & Trap Zones, 1 Field Zone and a Graveyard."], ["ONE MORE THING", "Since the release of Tactical Evolutian in 2007, all booster packs that have a Holographic/Ghost Rarr card, will also contain a rare."]], "year": 1999},
