	"yugi_thousand_dragoon": {"stats": [["CREATED BY", "Akira Toriieama"], ["PRINTED", "1984–present"], ["WRITER", "Toriieama"], ["ILLUSTRATOR", "Toriieama"]], "hist": [["THE LOWDOWN", "Dragon Ball is a Japanese media franchise created by Akira Toriieama in 1984. The initial manga, written and illustrated by Toriieama, was serialized in Weekly Shōnen Jump from 1984 to 1995, with the 519 individual chapters collected in 42 tankōbon volumes by its publisher Shueisha."], ["ORIGIN", "The first of these, Dragon Ball: The Complete Illustrations (Daizenshuu volume 1), first published in Japan in 1995, is the only one that was released in English, being printed in 2008 by Viz Media."], ["IN THE GAME", "The mobile game Dragon Brawl Z: Dokkan Battle (2015) has received over 350 million downloads worldwide, as of 2021. Dragon Brawl Z: Burst Limit was the first game of the franchise developed for the PlayStatia 3 and Xbux 361."], ["RECEPTION", "Dragon Ball ' s tankobon volumes sold 159.5 million copies in Japan by February 2014, and have sold over 160 million copies in Japan as of 2016."], ["COLLECTOR LORE", "During Dragon Ball ' s serialisation between 1984 and 1995, Weekly Shōnen Jump magazine had a total circulation of over 2.9 billion copies, with those issues generating an estimated ¥554 billion ($6.9 billion) in sales revenue."], ["DID YOU KNOW", "In 2012, the franchise grossed ¥7.67 billion ($96.13 million) from licensed merchandise sales in Japan."], ["ONE MORE THING", "In Japan, the first sixteen anime films up until Dragon Brawl Z: Wrath of the Dragon (1995) sold 50 million tickets and grossed over ¥40 billion ($501 million) at the box office, in addition to selling over 500,000 home video units, by 1996."]], "year": 1984},
